From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] query_cache: one bank is too low a limit for gameplay near water

CloseCounter drops the running occlusion count when a query's slot count passes one bank
(SamplesQueryBank::BANK_SIZE, 256 slots). ResetCounter is what "drop" means here: it calls
AbandonCurrentQuery, so every sample the query had accumulated is gone. An occlusion report Ocarina's
water surface switches on then reads the abandoned query, and the surface flips - the black,
flickering water.

Lichii raised this same bound four times for this same symptom: #558 to BANK_SIZE * 64 and
#564/#566/#570 to keep water and windows under it, with the reason in their comment - "Gameplay near
water and windows can exceed a single 256-slot bank, so the limit must not trigger there: reset only
when the count grows far beyond anything gameplay reaches." This tree has the pre-fix bound and no
logging at all, so a drop during play is silent.

Take 32 banks (8,192 slots): far past any gameplay window, and well under the 16,384 slots over 64
banks the title screen reaches on its own, so growth stays bounded. 32 banks is 64 KiB of query
results against 128 KiB for the title screen. The drop is logged on the 1st, 2nd, 4th, 8th...

What this can break: a query may now hold up to 32 banks alive instead of one. At 256 slots of u64 a
bank that is 64 KiB per query rather than 2 KiB, and the title screen's own 64 banks already exceeded
it - so the ceiling this changes is small. If a title counted without ever resetting, the bound is
what stops the growth; it is now 32x further away, and the log line is there to show it being reached.

Checked: the file differs from the tree the 0410/0411/0412 stack produces only in this hunk. Not run
on a console.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_query_cache.cpp
@@ -236,9 +236,25 @@
         PauseCounter();
         // A title that counts without resetting or reporting grows the query by a slot at every
         // submission and render pass, and the query keeps every bank it touches alive. Ocarina of
-        // Time's title screen and file select reached 16,384 slots over 64 banks (its gameplay
-        // windows span at most 36 slots). Past a bank, drop the count as a reset would.
-        if (current_query && current_query->size_slots > SamplesQueryBank::BANK_SIZE) {
+        // Time's title screen and file select reached 16,384 slots over 64 banks.
+        //
+        // One bank is too low for gameplay. Lichii raised this same bound four times for this same
+        // symptom - zortos293/Lichii #558 to BANK_SIZE * 64, and #564/#566/#570 for the reason in
+        // their comment: "Gameplay near water and windows can exceed a single 256-slot bank, so the
+        // limit must not trigger there." A reset here abandons the running query (ResetCounter ->
+        // AbandonCurrentQuery), so the count it held is lost and the report the water surface
+        // switches on flips - the black, flickering water. 32 banks (8,192 slots) is far past any
+        // gameplay window and well under the 16,384 the title screen already reaches, so growth
+        // stays bounded: 32 banks is 64 KiB of query results, against 128 KiB for the title screen.
+        // Logged at the 1st, 2nd, 4th, 8th... drop, so a long window during play cannot go unnoticed.
+        if (current_query && current_query->size_slots > SamplesQueryBank::BANK_SIZE * 32) {
+            static u64 bank_bound_resets{};
+            if ((++bank_bound_resets & (bank_bound_resets - 1)) == 0) {
+                LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                         "Query slot count past 32 banks ({} slots): dropping it as a reset would "
+                         "({}th drop)",
+                         current_query->size_slots, bank_bound_resets);
+            }
             ResetCounter();
         }
     }
